\newlabel{fig:class_dist}{{1}{7}{Class proportions (\%) in the full post-filter dataset ($N{=}103{,}915$), the imbalanced experimental subset ($N{=}1{,}000$), and the balanced subset ($N{=}1{,}000$). In the imbalanced condition, \texttt {credit\_reporting} is still the dominant class at 51.1\,\%, confirming that balanced evaluation is essential to avoid majority-class inflation}{figure.1}{}}
